ution:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\underbrace{e^{A(t-t_0)} \\, \\mathbf{x}(t_0)}_{\\text{homogeneous part}} + \\underbrace{\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{A(t-s)} \\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x(t_0)$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n![](images/ed/ed77716162d9ecdeee50cd26172985ed4a5038cad903ca4729da1d9895fc9cc4.svg)\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t = t_0 = 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x(0) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n![](images/22/22f92a117def6f3377a72f871d58d23cf339290a55c0f7d297ccb797b5046bf7.svg)\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3s+3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3s+3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-3s+3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\